**Summary of extraction:**

The Sui Framework (mainnet-v1.64.1) was analyzed across 12 core modules, yielding **58 program graphs** covering all security-critical functional units:

**Modules covered:**
- **balance** (6 graphs): Supply management, join/split, zero-destruction, staking rewards (system-only)
- **coin** (10 graphs): Currency creation (OTW-gated), mint/burn, split/join/divide, deny list v2, global pause, regulated currency, treasury-to-supply conversion
- **token** (8 graphs): Closed-loop token transfer/spend/to_coin/from_coin, request confirmation (immutable + mutable), flush spent balance, treasury cap bypass
- **kiosk** (8 graphs): Purchase (exact + PurchaseCap), take, list, lock, withdraw, close, borrow_val/return_val hot potato
- **transfer_policy** (4 graphs): Policy creation (Publisher-gated), rule management, request confirmation with receipt matching, destroy and withdraw
- **transfer** (4 graphs): Transfer/share/freeze/receive with bytecode verifier restrictions, party transfer
- **package** (4 graphs): Upgrade authorization (one-at-a-time), commit, policy restriction (one-way ratchet), Publisher claim (OTW)
- **random** (4 graphs): Generator creation (HMAC-SHA3-256 seeded), state update (system-only), range generation (bias-limited), Fisher-Yates shuffle
- **deny_list** (3 graphs): V2 add, V1 add (legacy), V1-to-V2 migration
- **kiosk_extension** (2 graphs): Extension installation, protected place
- **dynamic_field** (2 graphs): Add/remove with hash-based field IDs
- **pay** (1 graph): Join vector and transfer
- **object** (1 graph): UID creation

